2.1.m:
I instruct you especially, for you are dearest to me;
since you are a devotee of Viṣṇu, his devotee is exceedingly close to me.

The lord Rudra, the source of auspiciousness, instructed him repeatedly in this manner;
Nārada did not regard it as beneficial, deluded by the māyā of Śiva.

Kapālī with fifty million, the auspicious Sandāraka with sixty million, / and here Kaṇḍuka and Kuṇḍaka with tens of trillions;

Viṣṭambha went with eighty million, Candratāpana with eighty million;

the lord of the attendants Mahākeśa was surrounded by ten billion;
